<!-- ============ HOW I BUILT THIS ============ -->
<section class="build">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How I built this</p>
    <h2>From raw account data to an action a CSM can take</h2>
    <p>I built this end to end to show how I actually work a book of business — not just describe it. I started from a flat export of 48 B2B SaaS accounts and treated it the way a Customer Success or Client Operations team would: <b>model it, measure it, surface it, and act on it.</b> The dashboard below is populated from that same dataset, so the numbers on this page are the numbers in the data.</p>
    <p>The through-line is judgment at scale. SQL turns messy account data into a single defensible <b>health score</b> and a <b>dollar-weighted risk queue</b>; the dashboard makes that queue something a team can trust and re-sort in seconds; and an <b>agentic-AI layer</b> drafts the next move for each at-risk account — while a human stays the one who decides and sends. <span class="mute">Data is synthetic and every account name is fictional, so it is safe to share publicly.</span></p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h4>Model the data</h4>
        <p>Defined the account schema and a weighted composite health score from adoption, support load, sentiment and tenure.</p>
        <span class="tool">SQL · data modeling</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Find the risk</h4>
        <p>Ranked a churn-risk work queue by dollars &times; renewal urgency, and rolled the book up by CSM to balance coverage.</p>
        <span class="tool">SQL · aggregation</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Surface it</h4>
        <p>Turned the queries into a health &amp; renewal dashboard — KPIs, charts, and a filterable, sortable account table.</p>
        <span class="tool">Dashboard · HTML/JS/SVG</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Act on it</h4>
        <p>Designed agents that triage risk and draft save-plays, QBR prep and expansion outreach — human-in-the-loop by default.</p>
        <span class="tool">Agentic AI · human review</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

