<!-- ============ 2 · SQL ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="n">02</span><h2>The SQL behind the numbers</h2></div>
    <p class="sec-intro col">Every metric above is derived, not hand-entered. These are the queries a CSM/ops analyst would run against the account table — a health score composite, a churn-risk queue, and a QBR one-pager. They read against a table with the same columns as the dashboard below.</p>

    <div class="sql">
      <div class="bar"><span class="t">health_score.sql</span><span class="tag">composite score · 0–100</span></div>
<pre><span class="c">-- Weighted account health: adoption + support load + sentiment + sponsorship</span>
<span class="kw">SELECT</span>
  account, tier, csm, arr_usd,
  <span class="kw">ROUND</span>(
      0.45 * adoption_pct
    + 0.15 * <span class="kw">GREATEST</span>(0, 100 - open_tickets * 8)
    + 0.20 * (csat * 20)
    + 0.12 * ((nps + 100) / 2.0)
    + 0.08 * <span class="kw">CASE WHEN</span> exec_sponsor = 'Yes' <span class="kw">THEN</span> 100 <span class="kw">ELSE</span> 40 <span class="kw">END</span>
  , 1) <span class="kw">AS</span> health_score
<span class="kw">FROM</span> accounts
<span class="kw">ORDER BY</span> health_score <span class="kw">ASC</span>;</pre>
      <div class="why"><b>Why it matters:</b> one number the whole team trusts, built from signals a CSM can actually influence — so "unhealthy" always points at a lever, not just a mood.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="sql">
      <div class="bar"><span class="t">churn_risk_queue.sql</span><span class="tag">the daily work queue</span></div>
<pre><span class="c">-- Accounts to touch first: at-risk band, weighted by ARR and renewal urgency</span>
<span class="kw">SELECT</span>
  account, csm, arr_usd, health_score, renewal_in_days,
  <span class="kw">CASE</span>
    <span class="kw">WHEN</span> renewal_in_days &lt; 0            <span class="kw">THEN</span> 'OVERDUE'
    <span class="kw">WHEN</span> renewal_in_days &lt;= 90         <span class="kw">THEN</span> 'URGENT'
    <span class="kw">ELSE</span> 'MONITOR'
  <span class="kw">END</span> <span class="kw">AS</span> renewal_flag
<span class="kw">FROM</span> accounts
<span class="kw">WHERE</span> risk_band = 'At Risk'
   <span class="kw">OR</span> (health_score &lt; 60 <span class="kw">AND</span> renewal_in_days &lt;= 90)
<span class="kw">ORDER BY</span> (renewal_in_days &lt;= 90) <span class="kw">DESC</span>, arr_usd <span class="kw">DESC</span>;</pre>
      <div class="why"><b>Why it matters:</b> prioritization is the CSM's scarcest resource. This ranks the day's work by <b>dollars &times; urgency</b>, not by whoever emailed last.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="sql">
      <div class="bar"><span class="t">book_of_business.sql</span><span class="tag">CSM performance rollup</span></div>
<pre><span class="c">-- Portfolio view: coverage, average health, and at-risk load per CSM</span>
<span class="kw">SELECT</span>
  csm,
  <span class="kw">COUNT</span>(*)                                   <span class="kw">AS</span> accounts,
  <span class="kw">ROUND</span>(<span class="kw">SUM</span>(arr_usd) / 1000)                  <span class="kw">AS</span> arr_k,
  <span class="kw">ROUND</span>(<span class="kw">AVG</span>(health_score), 1)               <span class="kw">AS</span> avg_health,
  <span class="kw">SUM</span>(<span class="kw">CASE WHEN</span> risk_band = 'At Risk'
           <span class="kw">THEN</span> 1 <span class="kw">ELSE</span> 0 <span class="kw">END</span>)               <span class="kw">AS</span> at_risk
<span class="kw">FROM</span> accounts
<span class="kw">GROUP BY</span> csm
<span class="kw">ORDER BY</span> arr_k <span class="kw">DESC</span>;</pre>
      <div class="why"><b>Why it matters:</b> the same data that runs an account also balances a team — who is carrying the heaviest at-risk load, where to rebalance coverage.</div>
    </div>

    <p class="sec-intro col" style="margin-top:var(--s6)">Two of those queries are materialized directly below as the dashboard the team actually looks at.</p>

    <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top:var(--s5)">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Book of business — by CSM</h3>
        <p class="cap">Output of <span class="mono">book_of_business.sql</span></p>
<table class="afy-table">
<caption>Coverage and health per CSM (ARR in $K)</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">csm</th>
<th scope="col" class="num">accounts</th>
<th scope="col" class="num">arr_k</th>
