<!-- ============ 4 · AGENTIC AI ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="n">04</span><h2>The agentic-AI layer</h2></div>
    <p class="sec-intro col">The SQL finds the accounts; the dashboard shows them. The point of leverage in modern client operations is what happens <b>next</b> — and that is where a small crew of purpose-built agents earns its keep. Each one takes the queue as input and produces a reviewable draft, never an un-checked action.</p>

    <div class="flow" role="list" aria-label="Agentic workflow">
      <div class="node" role="listitem"><span class="st">STEP 01</span><h4>Signal ingest</h4><p>Nightly pull of usage, tickets, CSAT/NPS into the account table.</p></div>
      <div class="node" role="listitem"><span class="st">STEP 02</span><h4>Score &amp; rank</h4><p>SQL recomputes health and builds the churn-risk queue.</p></div>
      <div class="node ai" role="listitem"><span class="st">STEP 03 · AI</span><h4>Triage agent</h4><p>Reads the queue, clusters root causes, tags each account.</p></div>
      <div class="node ai" role="listitem"><span class="st">STEP 04 · AI</span><h4>Draft agent</h4><p>Writes the outreach / QBR / save-play draft for the CSM.</p></div>
      <div class="node" role="listitem"><span class="st">STEP 05</span><h4>CSM review</h4><p>Human edits, approves, sends. Outcome logged back to the table.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="agents">
      <div class="agent">
        <span class="tag">Agent · triage</span>
        <h3>Risk Triage Agent</h3>
        <p>Groups the at-risk queue by likely root cause — low adoption, support friction, lost sponsor, or pricing — so the CSM opens the day with a diagnosis, not a spreadsheet.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>input</dt><dd>churn_risk_queue.sql output</dd>
          <dt>signal</dt><dd>adoption ↓, tickets ↑, NPS &lt; 0</dd>
          <dt>output</dt><dd>root-cause tag + one-line rationale</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="agent">
        <span class="tag">Agent · drafting</span>
        <h3>Save-Play Drafting Agent</h3>
        <p>Turns a tagged risk into a specific play: re-onboarding invite, exec business review, or a value-recap email — pre-filled with the account's own numbers.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>input</dt><dd>account row + risk tag</dd>
          <dt>grounding</dt><dd>account facts only, no invention</dd>
          <dt>output</dt><dd>editable draft + suggested owner</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="agent">
        <span class="tag">Agent · prep</span>
        <h3>QBR Prep Agent</h3>
        <p>Assembles the quarterly-business-review one-pager: ARR trend, adoption story, open expansion, and the three talking points that matter for that specific account.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>input</dt><dd>book_of_business.sql + history</dd>
          <dt>output</dt><dd>QBR deck outline + metrics</dd>
          <dt>human</dt><dd>CSM confirms before the meeting</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="agent">
        <span class="tag">Agent · expansion</span>
        <h3>Expansion Scout Agent</h3>
        <p>Flags healthy, high-adoption accounts with headroom and drafts the expansion motion — the offensive counterpart to the churn queue.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>input</dt><dd>health &ge; 75, adoption &ge; 85</dd>
          <dt>output</dt><dd>upsell hypothesis + $ estimate</dd>
          <dt>routes to</dt><dd>CSM + AE for co-sell</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="src" style="margin-top:var(--s5)">Design principle: agents <b>draft and rank</b>; the CSM <b>decides and sends</b>. Every step is grounded in the account table so nothing is invented, and every action is logged back so the health score learns from the outcome.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 5 · PLAYBOOK ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="two">
      <div>
        <div class="sec-head"><span class="n">05</span><h2>The renewal-week playbook</h2></div>
        <p class="sec-intro">A checklist you can actually run — the operational spine that ties the SQL, the dashboard, and the agents into one weekly ritual.</p>
        <div class="playbook">
          <ol>
            <li><input type="checkbox" id="p1"><label class="txt" for="p1"><strong>Refresh the churn-risk queue</strong><span>Run the SQL; sort by dollars × urgency.</span></label></li>
            <li><input type="checkbox" id="p2"><label class="txt" for="p2"><strong>Review the triage agent's root-cause tags</strong><span>Confirm or correct each diagnosis.</span></label></li>
            <li><input type="checkbox" id="p3"><label class="txt" for="p3"><strong>Edit &amp; approve the save-play drafts</strong><span>Human voice on every outbound.</span></label></li>
            <li><input type="checkbox" id="p4"><label class="txt" for="p4"><strong>Lock QBR prep for accounts renewing ≤ 90 days</strong><span>One-pager + three talking points.</span></label></li>
            <li><input type="checkbox" id="p5"><label class="txt" for="p5"><strong>Route expansion-scout flags to AEs</strong><span>Play offense, not just defense.</span></label></li>
            <li><input type="checkbox" id="p6"><label class="txt" for="p6"><strong>Log outcomes back to the account table</strong><span>Close the loop; feed next week's score.</span></label></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>How to read this project</h3>
          <p class="cap" style="margin-bottom:var(--s3)">for a hiring manager</p>
          <p style="font-size:var(--step--1);color:var(--mute);line-height:1.55">This one page shows the full arc of a modern CS/client-ops role: <b style="color:var(--ink)">model the data in SQL</b>, <b style="color:var(--ink)">surface it in a dashboard</b> people trust, and <b style="color:var(--ink)">put an agentic-AI layer</b> on top to scale the human's judgment instead of replacing it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>Skills demonstrated</h3>
          <div class="legend" style="flex-direction:column;gap:var(--s2);margin-top:var(--s3)">
            <span>SQL — scoring, ranking, aggregation</span>
            <span>Dashboarding — live data, filters, charts</span>
            <span>Churn &amp; renewal risk management</span>
            <span>QBR &amp; expansion motion design</span>
            <span>Agentic-AI workflow design</span>
            <span>Human-in-the-loop governance</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

